@@ -2702,7 +2725,7 @@ entries:
     date: '1961-01-09'
     thread: china-leadership
     c: 'Chen Yun 陈云 directs the drafting of the Grain Price Small Group''s 中共中央粮价问题小组 report to Mao Zedong 毛泽东 and the Center 中共中央: grain purchase prices to rise 20 percent on average from this year (a billion yuan more for the peasants), of the 2.5 billion yuan of compensation only 1.5 billion paid in cash this year and a billion in People''s Bank 中国人民银行 promissory notes next year; with other farm prices up 25 percent on 26 to 30 billion yuan of sales, the peasants to gain 6.5 to 7 billion; oil, meat, poultry and eggs this year, cotton, tobacco, hemp, tea, sugar, timber and bamboo next; grain sale prices and wages unchanged for a year or two, the sale price in town below the purchase price in the country; state accumulation down over a billion this year, two billion next; townspeople to pay about 2 billion yuan more (6.5 percent of their purchasing power); of 9.5 billion yuan of currency out, institutions hold about 4 billion, townspeople 2.8 billion (21 yuan a head), peasants 2.7 billion (5 yuan a head); a gap of about 3 billion between purchasing power and goods, to be met with 1.5 billion more goods (150,000 tons more of rolled steel and 10 million dollars of light-industry materials).'
-    n: '[[w.chen-yun-nianpu-xiuding]], III, 65–67. See [[cal.1960-10.china-leadership-3]]. Made public: 2015. Names: Chen Yun.'
+    n: '[[w.chen-yun-nianpu-xiuding]], III, 65–67; [[w.jianguo-yilai-zhongyao-wenxian]], XIV, 60–66 (the report, "On raising the purchase price of grain" 《关于提高粮食收购价格问题的报告》, Jan. 9, 1961, to the Chairman and the Center, printed in full with the Center''s comment of Jan. 15). See [[cal.1960-10.china-leadership-3]]. Made public: 1997 ([[w.jianguo-yilai-zhongyao-wenxian]], XIV, 60–66). Names: Chen Yun.'
