@@ -4981,7 +5020,7 @@ entries:
     date: '1961-01-19'
     thread: china-leadership
     c: 'Chen Yun 陈云 speaks to the Central Work Conference 中共中央工作会议 on importing grain and drawing in currency: China must stand on its own grain, but two million tons can be imported now, the contracts nearly signed, and four million this year would ease things; walnuts, melon seeds and red dates to be exported for it, and a foot less cloth a head this year for a billion jin more grain: "one fist, not two"; cakes and sweets, cheap ones on coupons at five or six jiao a jin and dear ones for anyone with money, "one side of the net open", to calm people, nourish them and draw in money; imported sugar for fine sweets, imported wheat for cakes, the bran for pigs, and restaurants for fried pork; the capitalists'' interest at most 100 million yuan a year, 200,000 senior intellectuals, 50 million workers: the sweets will not run out, with over 100,000 tons of sugar landed, over 200,000 on the way and 300,000 more in the second quarter.'
