     c: 'Zhou Enlai at the joint meeting of the Propaganda Department''s literary and art symposium and the Culture Ministry''s film conference criticizes "left" thinking in arts work: "free the mind, break superstition, dare think, speak and act"; a democratic atmosphere; first change the style of cadres, leading cadres, "beginning with us few"; let others differ; no "putting on hats" and clubs. He treats the dialectic of material and spiritual production, class struggle and united front, whom and how to serve, art''s laws, heritage and creation, leadership and the masses, and asks them to criticize his talk as a "live target."'
